course: dictionary
lesson: 6685
title: Obsidian: a word from rocks and history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words get a special meaning in each subject. Obsidian is a noun, the name of a thing, so look at the words around it to find out what it is: «Obsidian is natural glass that forms when lava cools so fast that no crystals can grow.» The clues are natural glass and lava.
explain: Now read «Sharp volcanic glass called obsidian travelled hundreds of kilometres.» Volcanic tells you it comes from a volcano, and sharp tells you it can cut. Swap in your meaning: "sharp volcanic glass travelled hundreds of kilometres" still makes sense, so your idea is right.
explain: Words can change meaning between subjects. In science, obsidian is a rock made from cooled lava. In the game Minecraft, obsidian is a very hard block. Before you decide what a word means, ask which subject the text is about.
fact: Obsidian is a hard, shiny black or dark natural glass.
fact: Obsidian forms when lava from a volcano cools very quickly.
fact: Because it cools too fast for crystals to grow, obsidian is glassy.
fact: When obsidian breaks, it has very sharp curved edges.
fact: Long ago, people used obsidian to make very sharp knives, arrowheads and mirrors.
exercise: «Obsidian is natural glass that forms when lava cools so fast that no crystals can grow.» What forms obsidian? | Wood burned in a campfire | Sand washed up by the sea | *Lava that cools very quickly | Snow that melts slowly in spring
exercise: Obsidian was used long ago to make very sharp knives, arrowheads and mirrors. What could people make from obsidian? | *Sharp knives and mirrors | Cotton shirts | Soft pillows and blankets | Wooden boats for the sea
exercise: In the game Minecraft, what is obsidian? | *A very hard block | A kind of cloud | A soft green plant | A type of fish
test: «Sharp volcanic glass called obsidian travelled hundreds of kilometres.» What does volcanic mean here? | Made from wood | Coming from the sea | *Coming from a volcano | Very cold
test: Why is obsidian glassy and not made of crystals? | Because it was painted by people | *Because it cooled too fast for crystals to grow | Because it was heated for a whole year | Because it was frozen in ice
exam: «Obsidian, a sharp volcanic glass, was traded over long distances more than 10,000 years ago.» What does traded most likely mean? | Melted by the sun | *Bought, sold or exchanged | Broken into small pieces | Hidden deep in a cave
